    "max_raw_crossovers": 32768,
    "coordinate_bound": 1000000000000.0,
    "parallel_threshold": 1e-12
  },
  "assumptions": [
    "Adjacent acquisition samples form straight XY segments within each unique contiguous line_id. No sorting/reprojection, missing XY inference, line joining across runs or self-crossovers. All records need XY/line IDs; repeated/disjoint line IDs and consecutive segments <=2*intersection_tolerance require QC. Coordinates are bounded to +/-1e12 and units must be explicitly linear or resolved projected Cartesian.",
    "max_segment_length excludes geometry spanning acquisition gaps. X-bounds sweep and scaled cross products use binary64. Near-parallel/collinear overlap candidates are excluded at dimensionless 1e-12; min_crossing_angle is the acute angle in degrees. Explicit intersection_tolerance>=1e-9, <=1e6 and <=max_segment_length/100 snaps near endpoints and allows at most that XY separation, never extrapolating sample values.",
    "Shared-vertex intersections deduplicate by line/record/segment topology, not XY alone. Distinct repeat-path crossings remain distinct. Eligible representatives are preferred, then larger angle, then acquisition segment indices. Exact endpoint values/heights do not require a nonnull far endpoint; interior interpolation needs both. Null readings are never bridged.",
    "elevation_policy=ignore explicitly acknowledges XY-only comparison; native Z differences are informational, with no height reduction or comparability claim. limit requires nonnegative max_height_difference in declared linear height units plus known height_datum and up/down z_positive. Missing heights or excess differences make a crossover ineligible. No geoid/height conversion or external/temporal correction is inferred.",
    "Crossover difference is interpolated value_a-value_b. Ineligible comparisons remain visible with reasons. Resource failures return no partial crossing table. Binary64 numeric parity is tolerance-based; no exact-arithmetic claim.",
    "Fixed-reference levelling holds caller-designated reference lines at zero bias and fits each target with the equally weighted mean target-minus-reference crossover residual. One constant DC bias applies to every nonnull reading on a target, including beyond tie locations. This is an empirical fixed-reference strategy, not global network levelling, polynomial drift, outlier removal, microlevelling or geological interpretation.",
    "Every line must be explicitly classified reference/target. All targets must satisfy min_crossovers, min_reference_lines, max_abs_correction and max_rms_residual before one atomic magnetic_levelling event. Missing readings stay null; geometry/time, field type, order/extras/other channels remain. Native model/context binding supplements the existing observation binding. References/evidence and source corrections must be independently verified; no operation reordering or calibrated uncertainty propagation."
  ],
  "references": [
    "https://help.seequent.com/Oasismontaj/2023.2/Content/levelling/xlevel_gx.htm",
    "https://pubs.usgs.gov/of/2001/ofr-01-0145/data/dvalley-4254/655dvreport.pdf"
  ]
